"A level-triggered JK with J = K = 1 would keep toggling while the clock is high (race-around). A <b>master-slave</b> JK, built from two latches on opposite clock phases, avoids this.": "J = K = 1-সহ একটি level-triggered JK clock উঁচু থাকা পর্যন্ত toggle করতেই থাকত (race-around)। বিপরীত clock phase-এ দুটি latch দিয়ে তৈরি একটি <b>master-slave</b> JK এটি এড়ায়।",
